  <h1>A Generation of Children Grew Up Damaged by Their Soil</h1>
  <p class="dek">In the Great Lakes states before 1924, iodine deficiency was so common that schoolchildren carried visible goiters, and pregnant women were passing irreversible brain damage to their babies. The fix arrived in a grocery aisle.</p>
